A window's content is kept clear of the status bar and the display cutout
(`safeDrawingPadding`) however it reaches the Screen. Written directly in the
package body it is the Screen's children; under a reactive `if` the window is
an instance of its own (the implicit-state wrapper holding its `visible`), and
its content arrives through that instance's slot, rendered by the caller. The
inset belonged to the first route only, so the second drew under the status
bar, and its two nodes, handed to the Screen with no layout around them, drew
on top of each other.

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

var details = true

if details {
    ui.window(title="Inset") {
        ui.text(value="top")
        ui.text(value="below")
    }
}
